From 98eaa722c2a76313b1e36bfa040d9997c16f6edb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 09:11:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Store/kitchen countdown: transparent corners (no white band
 behind the card)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The countdown card is self-contained (own gradient, border, radius) but its
wrapping notice still painted a square surface, so its corners showed behind the
card's rounded ones — the four white/pale tips in the corners. That surface was
only neutralised on mobile; now it's neutralised on every viewport for the
kitchen-closing and store reopen/opening notices, so the corners are transparent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0187Jj4Q77V4UPawzEh9gsGr
---
 client/src/styles.css | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/client/src/styles.css b/client/src/styles.css
index b8417fc..714c3f4 100644
--- a/client/src/styles.css
+++ b/client/src/styles.css
@@ -2318,6 +2318,16 @@ body:has(.store-shell) { background: var(--bc-canvas-deep, #160f12); }
 .kc-cta, .kc-mcta { background: var(--bc-champagne); color: var(--bc-text-dark); }
 .kc-cta:hover, .kc-mcta:hover { filter: brightness(1.05); background: var(--bc-champagne-soft); }
 .kc-cta:focus-visible, .kc-mcta:focus-visible { outline-color: var(--bc-champagne); }
+/* The countdown card (kc-desktop / kc-tablet / kc-mobile) is self-contained —
+   its own gradient, border and radius. The wrapping notice must NOT paint its
+   own surface, or that square band shows its corners behind the card's rounded
+   ones (the "4 white tips in the corners"). Mobile already neutralised this; do
+   it on every viewport so tablet/desktop match. Overrides the --warning /
+   --urgent variant background these notices also carry. */
+.store-shell .site-notice--kitchen,
+.store-shell .site-notice--reopen {
+  background: none; border-top: none;
+}
 /* Thicker, fully-rounded progress: subdued champagne track, berry→coral fill. */
 .kc-progress { background: var(--progress-track); }
 .kc-progress-fill { background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--progress-fill-start), var(--progress-fill-end)); }
